A||||2||V6pack||Need swap info..'85 2.8 into an '87||||5||
Z||000000||V6pack||05-09-2000||01:48 AM||||Hi all.  I have a bad 2.8 in my '87 kit car and I have a good 2.8 in an '85 parts car.  Aside from a clutch disc/pressure plate change to go from a 4spd to the 5spd is there anything else that would prevent/make difficult swapping in the '85 engine ?<P>Will the ECM know the difference?  Is everything else the same?<P>Second question.  The '85 donor car also has a rebuilt front end with new shocks, rack, lowering sport springs, balljoints, etc.  It out-handles and out-rides the '87 front end. Can I unbolt this entire rebuilt '85 front suspension and bolt it into the '87 ?  <P>Need expert opinions :-))<BR>Thanks<BR>6pack <P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||05-09-2000||02:22 AM||||The short answer is....YES!  The engines are identical and the ECM should work just fine too.  The suspensions are identical and you will have no problems there either.<P>Your only concerns are with getting the proper clutch, but you already have that covered.||||reg||14
Z||000002||V6pack||05-09-2000||11:15 AM||||Thanks Mr. Fiero..I wasn't sure I could swap them out.  I am confident now!<BR>Thanks,<BR>V6pack||||reg||14
